    {
      "id": "s2-intro",
      "type": "intro",
      "label": null,
      "title": "IU — Through the Night(밤편지)",
      "content": "Expressing opinions softly. Koreans use this constantly.\n\n밤편지, literally 'a night letter,' is a quiet love song written as a message sent across distance in the dark. IU imagines sending a firefly toward someone's window as a stand-in for the words she can't fully say — 'I love you' — while comparing herself to handwriting in sand that the tide is slowly erasing.\n\nIn this lesson, you'll learn the grammar pattern **-(으)ㄹ 것 같다**, which means \"it seems like / I think.\" We'll see how IU uses it in \"Through the Night(밤편지).\"",
      "musicPlaying": true
    },
    {
      "id": "s3-intro",
      "type": "intro",
      "label": null,
      "title": "이번에 배울 것",
      "content": "이번 레슨에서 배울 단어:\n- **빛나다** — to shine\n- **울다** — to cry\n- **울 것 같다** — I think I'll cry\n- **좋아할 것 같다** — I think (they'll) like it\n\n레슨이 끝나면, 이 노래의 가사를 이해할 수 있어요.",
      "musicPlaying": true
    },
